  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">M&#xc4;N regional East</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">M&#xc4;N regionalt &#xd6;ST</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Impact objective: Increased gender equality and reduced gender-based violence in the Eastern Europe and South Caucasus region.

Programme objective: Targeted civil society actors in the Eastern Europe and South Caucasus region are effectively engaging men for gender equality, in redefining masculinity norms and in violence prevention, to ensure women&apos;s rights and security.

Expected outcomes:

1. Partner organisations in the EESC region have increased their strategic and operational capacity in working with engaging men for gender equality and against mens violence.

2. Targeted men in the EESC region take more responsibility for care and for unpaid domestic work.

3. Targeted men and boys in the EESC region challenge stereotypical masculinity norms and perceptions and are committed to preventing violence against women.

4. Feminist informed psycho-social support is accessible for targeted men and boys in the EESC region.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">M&#xe5;let med programmet &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos M&#xc4;Ns partnerorganisationer att involvera m&#xe4;n i j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsarbetet. Syftet &#xe4;r att minska m&#xe4;ns v&#xe5;ld mot kvinnor.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the Programme is to strenghten the capacity of M&#xc4;N&apos;s partners to engage men in gender equalty work. The aim is to reduce men&apos;s violence against women.</narrative>
  </description>
